# https://github.com/vercel/next.js/tree/canary/examples/cms-sanity#using-the-sanity-cli
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) for `next dev`. The project id and dataset
# are build-time public values: `next build` inlines them into the server and
# the Studio bundles. A deployed build takes them from its environment's
# SANITY_PROJECT_ID and SANITY_DATASET secrets (README → Connecting Sanity).
# Unset, the blog is unconnected: it renders its bundled sample posts under a
# "connect your Sanity project" notice, and /studio says how to connect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# Optional: production when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=
# The read token (draft mode / live preview only) is read at request time.
# Here it serves `next dev`; the Worker reads it as a secret — see
# .dev.vars.example. Optional: without it draft mode is refused with a 401.
SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=
# Optional. Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token (stands in for Vercel Speed
# Insights). Unset → no script is rendered.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=
